// Per-dimension tier semantics (GRA-98 / v0.5.0 survey rework).
//
// Schema is **provisional** — the Coder's `load_tier_table` loader
// and the corresponding `DimensionTier` (or equivalent) struct land
// in the Coder's next PR. The on-disk shape below matches the
// design doc's §6 (Progressive Survey Levels — Tier semantics per
// dimension) table; the Coder is free to amend the field names if
// a tighter schema lands during the loader PR.
//
// Each row says: "When a body's `DimensionFidelity` for `dimension`
// reaches `tier`, the player sees `description` in the dossier and
// the gameplay layer unlocks `unlocks`."
//
// Field reference (provisional):
//   `id`          — stable RON id, format
//                    "<dimension_ron_id>_t<tier>" (e.g.
//                    "MineralDeposits_t3"). Used by the dossier UI
//                    for tooltip lookup.
//   `dimension`   — one of the eight `SurveyDimension` ron_ids
//                    (OrbitalMech, Atmosphere, SurfaceFeatures,
//                    MineralClasses, MineralDeposits, Subsurface,
//                    Habitability, Anomalies)
//   `tier`        — 0..5; 0 = "none", 5 = "fully characterized"
//   `description` — one-line dossier tooltip for this (dimension,
//                    tier) combination. Drives the player's mental
//                    model of "what do I know at this tier?"
//   `unlocks`     — gameplay unlocks at this tier. Examples:
//                    "first_named_anomaly", "mining_unlocked",
//                    "drill_targettable", "biological_assay_ready".
//                    Empty list if purely informational.
//
// Source of truth: SURVEY_REWORK.md §6 (Tier semantics per dimension).
// The 8 × 6 = 48 rows below are a literal transcription of that
// table's right-hand columns, plus an `unlocks` interpretation that
// gates the gameplay effects the design calls out:
//
//   - MineralDeposits tier 2 = "suspected" (unlocks mining at 40%)
//   - MineralDeposits tier 3 = "first site pin"
//   - MineralDeposits tier 4 = "3 sites pinned" (unlocks full yield)
//   - Subsurface tier 3 = "shallow crust mapped" (unlocks
//     deep_drill targeting)
//   - Subsurface tier 5 = "mantle hints" (unlocks planetary bulk
//     mining at 20%)
//   - Atmosphere tier 3 = "breathability assessed" (unlocks
//     atmospheric gas mining at 60%)
//   - Anomalies tier 1 = "anomaly detected" (no name yet)
//   - Anomalies tier 2 = "first named anomaly" (UI surfaces id)
//
// Modder rebalance: edit `description` strings for narrative tone,
// or add new entries to `unlocks` to gate additional gameplay
// without recompiling.
(
    tier_table: [
        // ========== Orbital mechanics ==========
        (
            id: "OrbitalMech_t0",
            dimension: OrbitalMech,
            tier: 0,
            description: "No data.",
            unlocks: [],
        ),
        (
            id: "OrbitalMech_t1",
            dimension: OrbitalMech,
            tier: 1,
            description: "Mass, radius, orbit.",
            unlocks: ["orbital_insertion_unlocked"],
        ),
        (
            id: "OrbitalMech_t2",
            dimension: OrbitalMech,
            tier: 2,
            description: "+ axial tilt, rotation.",
            unlocks: [],
